From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Audit Hub <audit-hub@audit-hub.invalid>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 18:07:08 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 1/4] fix(api): make request ids from the system's
 cryptographic source

X-Request-Id came from Math.random, whose sequence is predictable: two
installations could repeat each other's ids, and anyone who saw a few
could guess the next ones. It now takes 128 bits from the system's
cryptographic source through expo-crypto, an Expo SDK module (installed
with `expo install`; 57.0.3, as 57.0.4 fails the supply-chain policy's
trust check). It is a native module: the next release is a store build.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
